  "coverage": [
    "A closed FSM can use one complete numeric loan across flat tuple payloads that share an exact prefix. Direct matrix payloads are represented as one managed prefix field. Every managed field occurs in every variant. The proof currently requires one complete Tail, a direct array result and no ordinary cold action; unsupported cases retain the maintained route.",
    "The compiler independently proves exact current tags at every payload observation, source CFG coverage, exact selected constructor factories, current array identities and functional versions across every state transition. Schema compatibility alone grants no ownership. No program names, measured times or particular payload contents select this code.",
    "Private tag words and normalized scalar fields reuse the same Cranelift scalar/frame emitter, numeric views, finite traversal schedule and first-change bridges. Entry branches on the checked original tag and imports only that variant's current physical scalar homes. Missing scalar suffixes are private zeros. Original disjoint managed homes retain the owners while the synchronous native loan is live.",
    "First-change transfers the exact current managed home into the maintained private matrix owner. On a resumable or successful boundary, dirty arrays freeze back into their entry homes before the new active payload is synchronized and inactive variants clear. The checked tag publishes last. Bounds, arithmetic, finite resources, immutable aliases, atomic output, cleanup and retry retain their established authority.",
    "Static source dataflow chooses the broader loan when it covers additional recurrent numeric work or another recurrent payload body, including scalar transition states. An existing constant-tag proof remains selected when it covers every recurring state. The stronger existing complete-tree preference and fast direct scalar entry remain maintained.",
    "Eight new original/decoded tests cover alternating tags, all seven numeric kinds and F64 bits, real native entry and Object/restored images, bounds/arithmetic failures after private updates, nine finite dimensions, distinct prior outputs, immutable aliases, zero per-state/cell library callbacks, exact metadata forgery rejection, old-version/foreign-root refusal, sticky entry refusal, cleanup/retry, constant-tag profitability and recurrent scalar-only transitions. One Engine test checks direct matrix projections and original disjoint homes."
  ],
  "development_checks": {
    "initial_training_probe_sha256": "42121f814fb23bfa25e553654f6076cb3af5d5c5eee6e12a4e76388e7bad8645",
