    "profitability_refinement": "The initial optimization-only replay improved Nussinov strongly but slowed Seidel. Seidel had one recurring numeric state and a terminal Done state. A general dataflow rule now retains the existing constant-tag proof when it covers every recurring state; a separate test requires complete loans across recurring scalar transition states. No holdout timing/profile was used for this choice. The initial replay and all regressions are retained.",
    "direct_payload_gap": "The first representation test showed that a single FSM payload such as Done(table) is a direct matrix, not a one-item tuple. The compiler projection and exact provenance/version transfer were extended; benchmark source was not rewritten.",
    "entry_transport_fix": "All-kind execution parity caught normalized scalar word zero colliding with the existing scalar-bank pointer. The final importer branches on the original current tag and loads its checked physical scalar homes directly. Both success and failure tests remain.",
    "fallback_tests": "The existing cold-entry/refusal fixtures use an incompatible payload order to retain their intended fixed-variant path. Broader complete-phase fallback is checked separately. A restored descriptor is reconstructed before the runtime-only refusal switch so independent source proof validation is not ablated.",
    "engine_log_reuse": "The195 Engine checks cover the final Engine sources. Later changes affect only GPU proof profitability and its tests; the unchanged Engine log is retained.",
